+THE ``already_occluded`` RENAME: CONSIDERED, DECLINED, AND WHY
+--------------------------------------------------------------
+A name is a claim, and this one has already misled a reader — so the decline is
+ARGUED, not assumed. A rename to something anchor-explicit (e.g.
+``occluded_by_this_anchor``) was considered and is DECLINED for three MEASURED
+reasons:
+
+1. A SWEEP IS MID-FLIGHT AND WILL EMIT A HEADER CARRYING THIS EXACT COLUMN.
+   :data:`TSV_COLUMNS` is the emitted header. Renaming now desynchronizes every
+   reader from an artifact already being written — including
+   ``pcs_panelwide_reclassify.py``, whose header check is STRICT EQUALITY
+   against :data:`TSV_COLUMNS` and would RAISE on the in-flight file.
+2. THE PRE-REGISTRATION NAMES THE TWO SUMMARY KEYS.
+   ``.planning/debug/260826-PCS-ancestry-blind-manifest-read-8x-duplication-and-the-prereg-prediction.md``
+   §(e) pre-registers ``n_undefined_already_occluded`` /
+   ``n_undefined_not_already_occluded``. Renaming a PRE-REGISTERED key in
+   response to a review is the exact move pre-registration exists to prevent.
+   The correct response to a misleading name whose semantics were misread is to
+   fix the SEMANTICS RECORD (this docstring) and to add the missing quantity
+   (the post-hoc tool) — not to relabel the prediction.
+3. ``TSV_COLUMNS IS PairResult._fields`` (a must-be-identity link). One rename
+   therefore moves the emitted header, :data:`SUMMARY_KEYS`, the banked BLOCK 2
+   identity pull and every downstream consumer AT ONCE.
+
+WHAT WOULD BREAK: the emitted TSV header; the two summary keys; the strict
+header equality check in ``pcs_panelwide_reclassify.py``; every banked
+``pcs_pairs.tsv`` already on disk; and the pre-registered key names.
+
+TRIGGER FOR REVISITING: the NEXT OSF version — and only AFTER the in-flight
+sweep lands and its artifacts are banked. Not before.
+
+ENFORCER (named, so this is not a belief):
+``tests/m3/test_pairwise_completeness_scan.py::test_the_already_occluded_rename_is_declined_while_the_sweep_artifact_contract_stands``
+fails if the field leaves the artifact contract while that contract stands.
+
